WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 6: People in Society.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:12.100
Unit 6 is about the people who keep a community
working: the helpers, the leaders, and the newcomers.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.820
You will meet a caretaker, a carpenter, an engineer and a
merchant, then governors, senators, lawyers and the military,

4
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:26.620
and finally artists, photographers, messengers,
refugees, immigrants, tenants and consumers.

5
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:33.460
You will use the Present Simple to say what each person
does, should and mustn't to give advice and rules,

6
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.400
prepositions to say where people go, and
the past tenses to retell what happened.

7
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.020
By the end you will describe the helpers in your own town,
just as Amal does in the story “The Community Parade”.

8
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.980
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.000
By the end of this unit,

10
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.660
you will be able to name and describe at least
twenty jobs and roles that people play in society.

11
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.760
You will also explain what different workers
and leaders do, using the Present Simple.

12
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.860
You will also give advice and state
rules using should and mustn't.

13
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.060
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:17.740
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: education,
celebration, competition, collection, admission, whereas.

15
00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.320
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.020
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.880
The reading sequence includes The People of Our
Town and Two Neighbours: A Refugee and an Immigrant.

18
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:35.360
Read actively.

19
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.840
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.880
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.620
The first language focus is Present
Simple: describing everyday jobs.

22
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.840
We use the Present Simple for routines,
facts, and things that happen again and again.

23
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:03.660
It suits jobs perfectly, because most jobs repeat every
day: “The caretaker cleans the school every morning.”

24
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.200
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.480
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Describe a Job.

26
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.180
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.680
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.800
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.360
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.440
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.780
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:44.560
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
